      "writtenOn": "2024-07-11T16:46:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To avoid doing the wrong thing if `clang --print-resource-dir` fails (e.g. using `/lib/baremetal/...` as the path to the library), we error here if the command failed. I\u0027ve tested that this works by teporarily doing `--xprint-resource-dir`, which results (as intended) in:\n\n```\n * Building FPMCU unittest binary for targets: bloonchipper                                                                             \nmake -j128 BOARD\u003dbloonchipper ALLOW_CONFIG\u003d1 TOUCHPAD_FW_DIR\u003d/build/${BOARD}/firmware clean \nclang: error: unknown argument \u0027--xprint-resource-dir\u0027; did you mean \u0027--print-resource-dir\u0027?\nclang: error: no input files   \ncore/cortex-m/build.mk:34: *** Could not determine path to libclang_rt.builtins.  Stop.                                                                                                                                                                                                  \n * ERROR: chromeos-base/chromeos-fpmcu-bloonchipper-unittests-9999::chromiumos failed (compile phase):\n *   emake failed                                                                                                                       \n```",
      "revId": "4242082cc9d256fe1545a8fc1ed2e7594b3ec0c8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    }
